# Line endings.
#
# The shell scripts here are run inside WSL, because that is where TrueForge
# runs. A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF, and
# bash then reads the carriage return as part of the command:
#
#   scripts/trueforge-up.sh: line 9: $'\r': command not found
#   scripts/trueforge-up.sh: line 18: syntax error: unexpected end of file
#
# The file looks perfect in every editor. Nothing in the repo is wrong. It is
# purely an artifact of how it was checked out, which makes it exactly the kind
# of failure someone hits on a fresh clone and cannot explain -- and the fresh
# clone is the case that matters, since it is how this project gets judged.
#
# So the scripts are pinned to LF regardless of platform or git config.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
